capability term/text-table  rows of cells under a header, the columns aligned by the cells their characters take on a terminal, drawn with lines or none
  heroes  term.format_table, term.Table, term.Align, term.Border
  go      tabwriter.Writer, tabwriter.NewWriter, tabwriter.Writer.Init, tabwriter.Writer.Write, tabwriter.Writer.Flush, tabwriter.AlignRight, tabwriter.Debug, tabwriter.DiscardEmptyColumns, tabwriter.TabIndent, tabwriter.FilterHTML, tabwriter.StripEscape, tabwriter.Escape
  rust    -
  python  rich.table.Table, rich.box
  note    a table is a value written to a `str` in one call, where tabwriter is a stream fed cells between tabs and flushed: its padding and minimum widths are the two spaces and the widest cell, `AlignRight` a column's `.right`, `Debug` the `|` of `.ascii`, `StripEscape` the style sequences a cell holds, which take no cell here; `DiscardEmptyColumns`, `TabIndent` and `FilterHTML` are a stream's concerns and left out. A column of numbers is right-aligned by itself (`.auto`), a decision where tabwriter and rich leave a column to the left unless told; borders none, a rule under the header, ASCII, the box-drawing characters and GitHub's Markdown. A control character in a cell is drawn as a space, so a row stays a line

